			<div class="content" id="post-content-3791623">
									

<p>This is a pretty interesting SCP! I had a couple of potential minor tonal edits.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Quick&nbsp;Edits</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3436 is contained within a 70&#160;m × 85&#160;m, 172&#160;m tall concrete building, which acts as a provisional site. The building — rectangular, beige, and with tinted windows — is designed to blend conspicuously with the surrounding metropolis.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The description of the building seems a little unnecessary, and you should probably call it &quot;Provisional Site-3436&quot; or such since it just contains one SCP. A potential edit might be as follows: &quot;Provisional Site-3436 has been built around SCP-3436, and has been designed to be as inconspicuous as possible.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>vermiform massing</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A quick Google search reveals that vermiform is more often used in anatomy and biology, so it seems a little out of place here. Replacing this phrase with &quot;worm-like&quot; may be better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>FWD: Evidence Regarding Origins</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What is the addendum on SCP-3436-i a forward of? Perhaps just leaving it as &quot;SCP-3436-i&quot; would be better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The series of statements loosely fits the format of a AWCY Project Proposal. Given that the original<br />
Project Proposal for SCP-3436 would have been presented to an intended patron prior to its<br />
completion, it is likely that the author intended SCP-3436-i as either an additional proposal to<br />
those who read it, or a meta-proposal intended for the religious deity it endorses.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The phrasing here is a little awkward, and AWCY? art installations don't necessarily have patrons, as far as I know. They usually would include at least one usage of the word &quot;cool&quot; as well, though that varies.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Selected Test Logs</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Testing logs usually follow a pretty specific format, so you might want to edit the formatting of the current one a bit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>On 07/04/1994, the same day a civilian trespassed upon the provisional site of SCP-3436 and<br />
experienced an unimpeded, pre-enclosure ABE,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You should note that there was some kind of containment breach, since SCP-3436 had apparently already been in containment before that date.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Otherwise, I like this SCP, though the addendum on SCP-3436-i could perhaps stand some more fleshing out and editing. I'm looking forward to seeing more of your writing in the future! +1</p>

							</div>

								
