														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3792684">
									

<p>I have to say, this article turned out to be nothing like what the picture made it thought it would be. I don't quite know how to express what I think of it as a whole, but I can say that I enjoyed the test results. Not just because they were unexpected (I thought that the D9Rs would go flying, but what happened was so much worse than that!), but I was probably irrationally pleased to see someone using a scientific layout for test results (abstract, results, conclusion/discussion).</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Small&nbsp;wording&nbsp;issue</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'd remove &quot;been&quot; from this sentence</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Access into the building is exclusive to the Site Director and accompanying Class C/D maintenance personnel who have been consented (Form 3436-A) and briefed to Level 2 security clearance.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I think I'll have to come back to it in a month or so and re-read it again to figure out what I think of it as a whole.</p>

							</div>

								
					
