<blockquote>
<p>I assume the bisection is from impacting the hook during the ABE</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yes, this was an occurrence that I intentionally didn't make explicit, very glad you picked up on it too.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the figures ascend being stopped and their still being alive just seems to introduce new information which doesn't point anywhere (though I suppose it implies the pulped bodies were still alive).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The event points backwards, to SCP-3436-i, which is a really gruesome interpretation of prophecies regarding &quot;the Rapture&quot;. Upon re-reading, the inscription becomes descriptive of the artist's ultimate endpoint for those who touch it.</p>
<p>So theoretically, there are several &quot;corpses&quot;/&quot;pulps&quot; stationary in the atmosphere that the Foundation has or has not yet incinerated.</p>

